WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.9 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Offboarding, handover and continuity

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Plan every exit so access is removed, knowledge stays and you learn why people leave.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Use an offboarding checklist with owners and dates.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Keep a short handover note for each key role.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Name who could cover each critical role.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Tide Line Youth Collective (Community group · idea stage, Indonesia)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“If Sari steps back, Wayan, trained the same way, becomes safeguarding focal person; the concern log is in a folder both can open.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write an offboarding checklist and a succession note.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
